Here are 5 specific, actionable recommendations for the Set circuit breakers on outgoing requests gate:

1. Implement a simple circuit breaker using a flag variable in the `RestTemplate` class located at `com.example.project.web.service.RestService.java`. Set this flag to true when an exception occurs while making an HTTP request and reset it to false after a successful response is received. This will ensure that subsequent requests are retried with exponential backoff if the circuit breaker is tripped.

Example code:
```java
public class RestService {
    private static boolean isCircuitBroken = false;

    public ResponseEntity<String> get(String url) {
        if (isCircuitBroken) {
            // Exponential backoff
            try {
                Thread.sleep(100);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE).body("Service unavailable");
        }

        RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();
        try {
            String response = restTemplate.getForObject(url, String.class);
            // Reset circuit breaker flag
            isCircuitBroken = false;
            return ResponseEntity.ok(response);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Set circuit breaker flag
            isCircuitBroken = true;
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```
